# How to Fold a Sitting Cat Origami

## Overview

This sitting cat origami creates a simple and recognizable paper cat with pointed ears, a geometric face, a rounded body, and an upright tail.

The model is folded from a single rectangular sheet of paper with a 1:2 ratio. No cutting or glue is required.

This page includes a complete 24-step origami diagram that can be viewed online or downloaded as a printable PDF.

## Result

![Pink sitting cat origami folded from a rectangular sheet](/diagram-images/sitting-cat-origami-diagram/pink-sitting-cat-origami.jpg)![Pink and red sitting cat origami models folded in two different sizes](/diagram-images/sitting-cat-origami-diagram/sitting-cat-origami-two-sizes.jpg)

The finished model forms a flat sitting cat silhouette that can be displayed upright. Different paper sizes can be used to create cats and kittens in matching colors.

