## Recommended Paper

For the best results, use:

- 15 × 7.5 cm or 20 × 10 cm rectangular paper
- Thin origami or kami paper
- Paper that holds sharp creases
- Solid colors that emphasize the cat silhouette

Larger paper is recommended for the first attempt because the layers around the ears and tail are easier to handle.

## Folding Tips

- Align the edges carefully during the initial pre-creases.
- Keep the central folds symmetrical to obtain an even head and body.
- Press the folds around the ears firmly to preserve their pointed shape.
- Adjust the final tail folds gently so the model can stand properly.
- Use different paper sizes to create a family of sitting origami cats.

## About This Diagram

This diagram presents the complete folding sequence in 24 illustrated steps. Standard origami symbols and arrows are used to make each movement easier to identify.

The PDF version provides a clear printable reference that can be followed without pausing or rewinding a video.

